From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:43:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Add a CPU scatter backend for graphics APIs without
 compute shaders

KSP on macOS renders with OpenGL 4.1, which has no compute shaders or
structured buffers, so the scatter system could not run there.

When SystemInfo.supportsComputeShaders is false, the Distribute and Evaluate
kernels of TerrainScatters.compute now run as Burst jobs:

- CpuScatterMath ports the kernel helpers and the three noise functions from
  gpu_noise_lib.glsl.
- CpuDistributeJob runs once per scatter per quad, like the Distribute kernel.
  Everything the Evaluate kernel derives per object that does not change frame
  to frame (orientation, random rotation, scale, terrain colour, despawn roll)
  is precomputed here.
- CpuEvaluateJob runs every frame per visible quad, frustum and range culls,
  and sorts the objects into LODs.
- The biome and block maps are read from their MapSO data, since KSP and
  Kopernicus compile them to unreadable textures.
- Each renderer uploads its LODs into RGBAFloat textures (4 texels per
  instance) and draws them with Graphics.DrawMeshInstancedProcedural, capped
  at the same counts as the GPU path's append buffers.
- Colliders get their positions straight from the distribute job instead of
  an async readback.

The GPU path is unchanged when compute shaders are available.
